>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `FORCE_TAC`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.FORCE_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by clarification, simplification, and best-first search.

`FORCE_TAC thms` clarifies with the current claset, performs
assumption-aware full simplification with the clasimpset, and solves every
residue with first-applicable-goal best-first search. Simplification is also
installed as an unsafe search wrapper.

The simp wrapper passed to clarification is deliberately inert:
clarification consults only safe wrappers, whereas `add_simp_wrapper`
installs an unsafe wrapper. The separate simplification step immediately
after clarification performs the intended simplification.

Unmarked theorems are inserted as assumptions. Classical markers modify
the temporary claset, `Simp` and `Iff` modify the temporary clasimp
context, and generic simplifier markers are passed to simplification.

### Failure

Fails unless the complete pipeline closes the goal. Malformed marked rules
can also fail during argument processing.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem force_tac_example:
  (p ==> q) ==> p ==> q
Proof
  clasimpLib.FORCE_TAC []
QED
```

